Package: BvChen
Type: Package
Title: Bivariate Chen Distribution: Properties, Estimation, and
    Applications
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mukul", "Bijalwan", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mukulbijalwan555@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-3040-6912")),
    person("Puneet Kumar", "Gupta", role = "aut",
           email = "puneetstat999@gmail.com")
    )
Description: Provides the density, cumulative distribution function,
    survival function, random number generation, hazard rate function,
    marginal and conditional distributions, statistical properties
    (joint moments, variance-covariance structure, Marshall-Olkin type
    survival copula, Kendall's tau and concordance ordering), maximum
    likelihood estimation through the expectation-maximization
    algorithm, Kolmogorov-Smirnov goodness-of-fit tests, Q-Q plots and
    contour and perspective visualizations for the bivariate extension
    of the bathtub-shaped Chen distribution of Gupta et al. (2022)
    <doi:10.1007/s41872-022-00193-4>. The model is constructed as
    min(Z1, Z2) of three independent latent Chen (2000)
    <doi:10.1016/S0167-7152(00)00046-9> components through competing
    risks, giving closed-form joint survival and conditional
    distributions and a singular component on the diagonal. Complete
    univariate Chen building blocks are included. Methods are based on
    Marshall and Olkin (1967) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1967.10498898>,
    Dempster et al. (1977) <doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1977.tb01600.x>,
    and Meintanis (2007) <doi:10.1016/j.jspi.2006.09.012>.
